let __v_935 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tomato\",\"tomatoes\",\"tomato sauce\",\"passata\",\"ketchup\",\"bolognese\",\"pasta sauce\"]},\"Tomato, and anything made with it, is one of the usual triggers, along with chilli, onion, garlic, citrus, chocolate and alcohol: they loosen the valve at the top of the stomach, so acid travels back up. Cut back on it for a fortnight and the heartburn usually eases, and an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) settles a bad night within minutes. See a GP if it lasts more than three weeks.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"spicy\",\"spice\",\"spices\",\"curry\",\"curries\",\"chilli\",\"chilli sauce\",\"chili\",\"hot sauce\",\"hot food\",\"jalapeno\",\"jalapenos\",\"vindaloo\",\"tikka\",\"naga\"]},\"Chilli and curry are the usual triggers, along with onion, garlic, citrus, chocolate and alcohol: they loosen the valve at the top of the stomach, so acid travels back up. A plain rice or bread with it soaks some of it up, and an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) settles a bad night within minutes. See a GP if it lasts more than three weeks.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"citrus\",\"orange\",\"oranges\",\"orange juice\",\"lemon\",\"lemons\",\"grapefruit\",\"lime\",\"satsuma\",\"clementine\"]},\"Citrus is one of the usual triggers, along with tomato, chilli, onion, garlic, chocolate and alcohol: they loosen the valve at the top of the stomach, so acid travels back up. Cut back on it for a fortnight and the heartburn usually eases, and an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) settles a bad night within minutes. See a GP if it lasts more than three weeks.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"onion\",\"onions\",\"garlic\",\"shallot\",\"shallots\",\"leek\",\"leeks\"]},\"Onion and garlic are two of the usual triggers, along with tomato, chilli, citrus, chocolate and alcohol: they loosen the valve at the top of the stomach, so acid travels back up. Cooking them well softens the effect for a lot of people, and an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) settles a bad night within minutes. See a GP if it lasts more than three weeks.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"fried\",\"frying\",\"fatty\",\"greasy\",\"chips\",\"batter\",\"pizza\",\"cheese\",\"cream\",\"takeaway\"]},\"Fried and fatty food is one of the usual triggers, along with tomato, chilli, onion, garlic, citrus and alcohol: fat slows the stomach down, so the acid has longer to travel back up. Grilling rather than frying helps, and an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) settles a bad night within minutes. See a GP if it lasts more than three weeks.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"mint\",\"mint tea\",\"peppermint\",\"peppermint tea\",\"spearmint\",\"after dinner mint\",\"polos\"]},\"Mint is a quiet trigger: it relaxes the valve at the top of the stomach, so the peppermint tea people drink for a bad stomach can make heartburn worse. Swap it for camomile or ginger, and an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) settles a bad night within minutes. See a GP if it lasts more than three weeks.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"coffee\",\"espresso\",\"latte\",\"cappuccino\",\"caffeine\",\"cola\",\"energy drink\"]},\"Coffee is one of the usual triggers, along with alcohol, tomato, chilli, onion, citrus and chocolate: caffeine loosens the valve at the top of the stomach, so acid travels back up. Two cups a day is usually fine and four is usually not, and an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) settles a bad night within minutes. See a GP if it lasts more than three weeks.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"wine\",\"beer\",\"lager\",\"alcohol\",\"vodka\",\"gin\",\"cider\",\"prosecco\",\"whisky\",\"whiskey\",\"brandy\",\"cocktail\",\"cocktails\"]},\"Alcohol is one of the usual triggers, along with tomato, chilli, onion, garlic, citrus and chocolate: it loosens the valve at the top of the stomach, so acid travels back up. Drinking earlier in the evening and less of it is what helps most, and an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) settles a bad night within minutes. See a GP if it lasts more than three weeks.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chocolate\"]},\"Chocolate is one of the usual triggers, along with alcohol, tomato, chilli, onion, citrus and coffee: it loosens the valve at the top of the stomach, so acid travels back up. Keeping it to the afternoon rather than the evening helps, and an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) settles a bad night within minutes. See a GP if it lasts more than three weeks.\"]}]}")?;
