let __v_942 = Value::from("A ring of muscle where the food pipe meets the stomach keeps the acid down, and heartburn is that ring relaxing at the wrong moment so acid travels back up and burns. Big or late meals, fatty and spicy food, alcohol, coffee, chocolate, mint and extra weight all loosen it. Eating smaller and earlier, and raising the head of the bed 10 to 15cm, is what settles it; an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) covers a bad night in minutes.");
frame.store("_HEARTBURN_WHY", __v_942.clone())?;
let __v_943 = Value::from("Tomato and tomato sauces, chilli and curry, onion and garlic, citrus, fried and fatty food, chocolate, mint, coffee and alcohol are the usual ones, and which of them matter is personal. Write down what you ate on the bad nights for a fortnight and two or three will stand out; cut those back and it usually eases, with an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) settling a bad night in minutes.");
frame.store("_HEARTBURN_WHICH", __v_943.clone())?;
