let __v_1081 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"scab\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"scab\",\"scabs\",\"scabbing\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"made of\",\"made\",\"form\",\"forms\",\"fall off\",\"falls off\",\"heal\",\"heals\",\"healing\"]},\"A scab is a plug of dried blood, platelets and a stringy protein called fibrin that seals a cut while new skin grows underneath it. Leave it alone - it is the dressing - because picking it off reopens the wound and makes a scar more likely, and the itch under it is new skin and nerve endings knitting back. A scab with spreading redness, heat or pus around it is the one to get looked at.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"weeping\",\"oozing\",\"smell\",\"smells\",\"yellow\",\"green\",\"hot\",\"red\",\"sore\",\"painful\",\"knee\",\"arm\",\"face\",\"head\",\"child\",\"baby\",\"bleeding\",\"infected\",\"infection\",\"looks infected\",\"getting infected\",\"mouth\",\"in my mouth\",\"in the mouth\",\"gum\",\"gums\",\"tongue\",\"lip\"]}]}],[\"blister\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"blister\",\"blisters\",\"blistering\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"come from\",\"form\",\"forms\",\"cause\",\"causes\",\"heal\",\"heals\"]},\"A blister is fluid trapped under a separated top layer of skin, usually from friction, heat or a burn, and the fluid is serum protecting the new skin underneath. Leave it whole and cover it loosely - popping it invites infection - and if it bursts on its own keep it clean and put a plaster on it. A burn blister bigger than a 50p, or any blister with spreading redness, wants a pharmacist or GP.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"burns\",\"burn\",\"scald\",\"scalded\",\"pop\",\"popped\",\"popping\",\"burst\",\"bursting\",\"drain\",\"lance\",\"should i\",\"can i\",\"prevent\",\"prevents\",\"preventing\",\"stop\",\"stops\",\"stopping\",\"avoid\",\"avoiding\",\"not get\",\"from getting\",\"feet\",\"foot\",\"heel\",\"toe\",\"shoe\",\"shoes\",\"running\",\"walking\",\"hand\",\"finger\",\"mouth\",\"cold sore\"]}]}],[\"plaque\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"plaque\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"teeth\",\"teeth mean\",\"gum\",\"gums\",\"tartar\",\"brush\",\"brushing\",\"remove\",\"get rid\",\"build up\",\"buildup\",\"cause\",\"causes\",\"bad\"]},\"Plaque is the soft, sticky film of bacteria that forms on teeth within hours of brushing, feeding on sugar and making the acid that causes decay and sore gums. Brushing twice a day with fluoride toothpaste and cleaning between the teeth once a day shifts it, and once it hardens into tartar only a dentist can scale it off. Blood on the toothbrush is the sign gum inflammation has started.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"artery\",\"arteries\",\"heart\",\"brain\",\"skin\",\"psoriasis\",\"how often\",\"electric\",\"toothbrush\"]}]}],[\"mole\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"mole\",\"moles\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"check\",\"checks\",\"normal\",\"dangerous\",\"cancer\",\"remove\",\"removed\",\"new\",\"changing\",\"changed\",\"grow\",\"growing\",\"itch\",\"itchy\",\"bleed\",\"bleeding\"]},\"A mole is a small cluster of pigment cells, the kind you are born with or that arrive slowly over years, and almost all are harmless. The check is the alphabet one: Asymmetry, a ragged Border, more than one Colour, a Diameter over 6mm, and anything Evolving in size, shape or itch. A new dark spot, or a mole that changes over weeks, wants a GP look rather than a wait.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"on my back\",\"my back\",\"shoulder\",\"arm\",\"leg\",\"face\",\"removed\",\"shave\",\"garden\",\"grass\",\"in the garden\",\"lawn\",\"yard\"]}]}],[\"callus\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"callus\",\"calluses\",\"callous\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"form\",\"forms\",\"cause\",\"causes\",\"remove\",\"get rid\",\"treat\",\"hard\",\"skin\",\"why\"]},\"A callus is thickened skin built where repeated pressure or friction makes the skin protect itself: hands from tools, weights or a guitar, feet from tight shoes. File it gently after a bath and use gloves or better-fitting shoes so it stops coming back, and don't cut it with a blade. A painful hard lump on a foot, or any foot callus with diabetes, is a podiatrist's job.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"feet\",\"foot\",\"heel\",\"toe\",\"shoe\",\"shoes\",\"running\",\"diabetes\",\"hand\",\"hands\",\"guitar\",\"weight\",\"weights\",\"deadlift\",\"gym\",\"painful\",\"pain\",\"hurts\",\"hurt\",\"sore\",\"aching\",\"aches\",\"bleeding\",\"cracked\",\"split\",\"infected\"]}]}],[\"cough\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cough\",\"coughs\",\"coughing\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"dry\",\"chesty\",\"wet\",\"cause\",\"causes\",\"why\",\"what does\",\"mean\",\"normal\",\"how long\",\"last\"]},\"A cough is a reflex that clears the airway: a quick breath in, the vocal cords shut, and air is forced out to shift mucus, dust or an irritant. Most coughs after a cold are viral and settle in two to three weeks, and honey in warm water eases the tickle. A cough with breathlessness, blood, chest pain, or one that lasts over three weeks needs a GP.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"child\",\"baby\",\"kid\",\"toddler\",\"son\",\"daughter\",\"night\",\"at night\",\"cant stop\",\"can't stop\",\"wont stop\",\"won't stop\",\"medicine\",\"syrup\",\"antibiotic\",\"antibiotics\",\"get rid\",\"stop\",\"treat\",\"smoker\",\"smoking\",\"vape\",\"asthma\",\"covid\",\"chest infection\",\"fever\"]}]}],[\"immunity\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"immunity\",\"immune system\",\"immune\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"how does\",\"how do\",\"what is\",\"work\",\"works\",\"build\",\"boost\",\"stronger\",\"low\",\"weak\",\"mean\"]},\"Immunity is your body's memory of a germ: white blood cells that have met a virus or a vaccine keep a record of its shape, so the next meeting is fought off before it makes you ill. That is why some illnesses you only get once and why a vaccine works without the disease, and why some of it fades over years - which is what tetanus and flu boosters are for.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"boost\",\"boosting\",\"supplement\",\"supplements\",\"vitamin\",\"vitamins\",\"weak\",\"compromised\",\"autoimmune\",\"hiv\",\"chemo\",\"steroid\",\"steroids\"]}]}],[\"stitch\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"stitch\",\"stitches\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"what is\",\"whats a\",\"what's a\",\"explain\",\"mean\"]},\"A stitch is a cramp-like pain in the side, from the diaphragm and the ligaments holding it being pulled while you breathe hard - most often in running. Slow down, breathe out fully, and press a hand into the sore spot; it usually eases in a minute or two, and building distance up gradually stops it coming back. Pain that stays after you stop, or comes with vomiting, is not a stitch.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"get rid\",\"stop\",\"prevent\",\"why\",\"cause\",\"causes\",\"running\",\"run\",\"when i run\",\"while running\",\"side\",\"in my side\",\"in the side\",\"avoid\",\"wound\",\"cut\",\"surgery\",\"operation\",\"scar\",\"healing\",\"after birth\",\"perineum\",\"dissolvable\",\"removed\",\"nurse\",\"hospital\",\"a&e\",\"children\",\"child\",\"knitted\"]}]}],[\"tonsils\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tonsils\",\"tonsil\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"what are\",\"what do\",\"do\",\"for\",\"removed\",\"out\",\"why\"]},\"The tonsils are two lumps of lymph tissue at the back of the throat that catch germs coming in through the mouth and nose, and they swell while they are fighting an infection. They shrink with age, which is why an adult's are small; very large ones in a child that cause snoring or pauses in breathing, or tonsillitis again and again, are what gets a referral.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"swollen\",\"swelling\",\"big\",\"large\",\"enlarged\",\"lumpy\",\"sore\",\"painful\",\"hurts\",\"hurt\",\"throat\",\"swallowing\",\"fever\",\"white\",\"spots\",\"pus\",\"child\",\"son\",\"daughter\",\"kid\",\"tonsillitis\",\"antibiotic\",\"antibiotics\",\"should i\",\"get them\"]}]}],[\"sneeze\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sneeze\",\"sneezes\",\"sneezing\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"why\",\"cause\",\"causes\",\"what\",\"happen\",\"happens\",\"twice\",\"three times\",\"in a row\",\"sunlight\",\"light\"]},\"A sneeze is a reflex that clears the nose: dust, pollen or a virus irritates the lining and the body takes a sharp breath and blasts air out to shift it. The droplets fly several metres, which is why you catch it in your elbow rather than your hand, and bright light makes some people sneeze.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"cant stop\",\"can't stop\",\"wont stop\",\"won't stop\",\"hayfever\",\"hay fever\",\"allergy\",\"allergies\",\"pollen\",\"cold\",\"flu\",\"covid\",\"snot\",\"blocked\",\"medicine\",\"antihistamine\",\"tablet\",\"tablets\",\"sun\",\"sunlight\",\"sunshine\",\"light\",\"bright\",\"in the sun\",\"in the light\",\"photic\"]}]}]]}")?;
